<title>USA: Carver against stockholder proposal to sell.</title>
<headline>Carver against stockholder proposal to sell.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-06-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Carver Bancorp Inc said Friday that it has received a stockholder proposal from Joseph Sonnenberg regarding a non-binding resolution to put the company up for sale.</p>
<p>Carver, the holding company for Carver Federal Savings Bank, said its board has unanimously voted to recommend that stockholders vote against the proposal.</p>
<p>The company said it will include a statement in opposition to the stockholder proposal in the company's proxy statement, which is scheduled to be mailed in mid-July.</p>
</text>
